    <h2>FAQ</h2>

    <h3>Is ChatGPT better than Gemini?</h3>
    <p>ChatGPT is better for general-purpose writing, coding assistance, and custom GPT workflows. Gemini is better for research, multimodal tasks, and Google Workspace integration. For most users who want a versatile AI assistant, ChatGPT Plus wins. For users who live in Google Workspace and need real-time web access, Gemini wins.</p>

    <h3>Which is cheaper, ChatGPT or Gemini?</h3>
    <p>Gemini is slightly cheaper. Google AI One Premium costs $19.99 per month and includes Gemini 2.5 Pro plus 2 TB Drive storage and Gemini in Gmail and Docs. ChatGPT Plus costs $20 per month and only includes ChatGPT access. If you already pay for Google Workspace, Gemini is effectively cheaper because the bundle replaces other subscriptions.</p>

    <h3>Which has a larger context window?</h3>
    <p>Gemini 2.5 Pro has the larger context window at 2 million tokens, the largest among consumer AI assistants in 2026. ChatGPT Plus with GPT-4 Turbo supports 128K tokens. For users who need to process very long documents, codebases, or videos, Gemini wins by a wide margin.</p>

    <h3>Which is better for coding?</h3>
    <p>ChatGPT is generally better for coding. GPT-4 Turbo and o1 produce more accurate code, handle complex refactors better, and the Advanced Data Analysis sandbox lets ChatGPT execute Python code. Gemini matches ChatGPT on short scripts and benefits from Google tooling integration, but ChatGPT is the safer choice for production code work.</p>

    <h3>Can ChatGPT access the internet?</h3>
    <p>Yes, ChatGPT Plus has built-in web search through Bing integration that runs automatically when needed. Gemini also has built-in Google Search integration that runs by default. Both tools can access current information, but Gemini's Google Search integration is faster and more comprehensive for research tasks.</p>

    <h3>Can I use ChatGPT and Gemini together?</h3>
    <p>Yes, and many professionals do. A common workflow is to use Gemini for research and data-heavy drafts because of its 2 million token window and built-in Google Search, then refine the output in ChatGPT for final polish and custom GPT workflows. The combined monthly cost is around $40, which is still less than a single hour of freelance writer or developer time.</p>

